+++ b/.changeset/compare-experiments-paired-delta.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+'@mastra/core': minor
+---
+
+`compareExperiments` computes `delta` over the items scored in both experiments whose target run did not fail in either (new `pairedCount`), instead of subtracting each experiment's own mean. Before, a candidate that ran fewer items, or failed on the hardest ones, was compared on a different set of items and could show a regression or an improvement that came only from the item mix. `statsA` and `statsB` still describe each whole experiment, so `statsB.avgScore - statsA.avgScore` can differ from `delta`. A warning names experiments that ran different items.
